# The dashboard UI under pkg/dashboard/ui is a generated Vite build output. It is
# committed (not gitignored) because it is //go:embed-ed into the binary so
# `go install`, the Docker image and releases ship a working dashboard without
# Node. It is rebuilt by `make ui-build` and gated by `ci-ui-drift`, so it is
# never hand-edited.
#
# `linguist-generated=true` collapses these files in GitHub diffs and excludes
# them from Linguist language stats and classic CodeQL code scanning. NOTE: it
# does NOT suppress GitHub's newer "Code Quality" bot (github-code-quality),
# which currently has no path-ignore and still flags the minified vendor chunks
# (e.g. spurious "semicolon insertion" on mermaid). That check is non-blocking
# (not in the CI `required` set); its threads are resolved as generated-vendor
# noise, never by editing these files.
#
# `-whitespace` unsets Git's whitespace-error checking for the same paths, so
# `git diff --check` stops failing on the minifier's output. The bundles carry
# trailing whitespace inside minified string and template literals, where it is
# content rather than sloppiness: it is what the source asked for, and stripping
# it would change what the browser renders. The only two ways to "fix" it are to
# hand-edit a generated file or to weaken the check for the whole repository,
# and both are worse than telling Git the truth about these paths. The scope is
# exactly the generated tree, so every authored file — Go, Svelte, TypeScript,
# Markdown, YAML — is still whitespace-checked. Drift in this tree is caught by
# `ci-ui-drift` rebuilding it, which is the gate that actually applies here.
pkg/dashboard/ui/** linguist-generated=true -whitespace
